{
  "id": "sublime",
  "name": "Sublime Text",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Development",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "sublime_text.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.sublimetext.4"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://www.sublimetext.com/docs/",
    "https://www.sublimetext.com/docs/key_bindings.html",
    "https://docs.sublimetext.io/reference/keyboard_shortcuts_win.html",
    "https://docs.sublimetext.io/reference/keyboard_shortcuts_osx.html"
  ],
  "note": "Sublime Text 4. Taken from the key bindings Sublime ships inside Packages/Default.sublime-package - Default (Windows).sublime-keymap and Default (OSX).sublime-keymap - labelled with the captions from Main.sublime-menu, covering the File, Edit, Selection, Find, View, Goto and Tools menus. Only unconditional bindings are used; entries carrying a `context` clause are situational overrides and are left out. Numpad-only bindings (keypad_enter, keypad_plus, keypad_minus) and bindings on keys the chord grammar has no name for (quote, parenthesis and brace auto-pairing) are dropped. Where Sublime ships more than one unconditional binding for a command (Ctrl+C and Ctrl+Insert for copy) the one built on the platform's primary modifier is listed. Nested menu entries are named \"Submenu: Command\"; menu entries that carry no caption of their own take Sublime's own derived caption (the command name in title case). Menu entries whose label is dynamic - the recent-file, open-file, bookmark and build-system lists - are omitted.",
